// The syntax errors a chain binding can produce (revision 1.4, spec 7.4).
//
// A binding is "PIN <connector> <segment>", so what follows a connector has
// to be a segment. '?' is not one: spec 11.6 spells the deliberate float
// "PIN = ?" and only '=' takes it, because the other three connectors join a
// run of elements and there is no run to join to nothing.
block binding-syntax {
    {U1~SOME-PART:
        A == ?;
    };
};
